{
"dur": 44.024,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 6.158,
"text": "Since 2000, Putin has spent much of his time at Novo-Ogaryovo, a guarded estate in the forest west of Moscow.",
"end": 6.433
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 6.433,
"vo_start": 6.708,
"vo_end": 11.624,
"text": "He also spends long stretches at a lakeside residence at Valdai, between Moscow and St Petersburg.",
"end": 11.899
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 11.899,
"vo_start": 12.174,
"vo_end": 21.374,
"text": "There is a summer residence at Sochi on the Black Sea, and a huge palace on the coast at Cape Idokopas that investigators link to him. He denies owning it.",
"end": 21.649
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 21.649,
"vo_start": 21.924,
"vo_end": 27.185,
"text": "Having many homes is useful. But to get between them, or to meet other leaders, he has to travel.",
"end": 27.46
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 27.46,
"vo_start": 27.735,
"vo_end": 31.095,
"text": "And a leader on the move is a leader at his most exposed.",
"end": 31.37
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 31.37,
"vo_start": 31.645,
"vo_end": 36.724,
"text": "He is guarded day and night by uniformed officers and by plain-clothes agents you would never notice.",
"end": 36.999
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 36.999,
"vo_start": 37.274,
"vo_end": 43.074,
"text": "But the Kremlin's security leans on one idea above everything else: nobody should be able to predict where he will be.",
"end": 44.024
}
],
